<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105859" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύλος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύλη</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i>callus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				1.2.54
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				178
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.80
			</span></i>; inside the hands, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὼ χεῖρε τύλων ἀνάπλεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Somn.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			; on the knees, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				553
			</span></i>, etc.; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυλόω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>anything rising like a lump, knob</i> or <i>knot</i>; esp.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>wooden bolt with a knob at the end, trenail,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				553
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				82
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>An.</u>
				2.3.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>knob</i> on a club, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥόπαλον τύλους ἔχον περισιδήρους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					3.33
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				16.4.17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>membrum virile,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.176
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>knob</i> or <i>nose</i> on which the thread of a screw works,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hero
				<u>Spir.</u>
				1.5
			</span></i>; <i>peg</i> on which a string is looped, <i><span class="en">
				Eutoc.
			</span></i> ad <i><span class="en">
				Archim.
			</span></i> iii <i><span class="en">
				p.60
			</span></i> H.; <i>knob</i> on an axle to which a cord is attached, <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				49.3.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				49.4.25
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				51
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				49.8.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.68
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ</span> Nic.l.c.; cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύλη.</span>]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
